# Tile overlay widgets (client/MANIFEST.md "game_tileoverlays", BASE.md 21): a tile drew one widget (Tile:setWidget, taken by the ground loot labels), so a second module could not draw over the same tile. Tile:addOverlayWidget(widget) / removeOverlayWidget(widget) / hasOverlayWidget(widget) / getOverlayWidgets() keep a short list of more widgets that Tile::drawWidget draws after the setWidget one, placed the same way (centred on the tile, moved by their margins), so they follow walking, scrolling, zoom and floor changes and take no input. Lua owns them: Tile::clean forgets them without destroying them (the module puts them on the rebuilt tile). Also the option "Field timers over magic walls and fields" (fieldTimers, on by default) in a new panel after "Keep attacking while moving" in Options > Interface; its apply hands the value to game_tileoverlays. Touches src/client/tile.h/.cpp, luafunctions_client.cpp, client_settings dataset.lua and options/interface.otui.
